{"name":"Bloodstone Village","status":"ok","title":"Bloodstone Village","pageId":12695,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"dablink\" style=\"padding-left:2em;\"><i>This article is about the settlement sometimes called Bloodstone Gate. For for the similarly named fortifications, see <a href=\"/wiki/Bloodstone_Gates\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Bloodstone Gates\">Bloodstone Gates</a>.</i></div>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Bloodstone Village</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society<sup id=\"cite_ref-tBL-p26_4-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tBL-p26-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Dwarves\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dwarves\">Dwarves</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Half-orc\" title=\"Half-orc\">half-orcs</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Halfling\" title=\"Halfling\">halflings</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">humans</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"alignment\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Alignments</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">All</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Commerce</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"imports\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Imports</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Food, livestock, wood</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"exports\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Exports</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Bloodstones</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Politics</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"government\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Monarchy (formerly)</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruler</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">King <a href=\"/wiki/Gareth_Dragonsbane\" title=\"Gareth Dragonsbane\">Gareth Dragonsbane</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">0 <small>(<a href=\"/wiki/Warlock_Knights\" title=\"Warlock Knights\">Warlock Knights</a> garrison)</small><sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1480_DR\" title=\"1480 DR\">1480&#160;DR</a><br>13,233<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p107_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p107-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372&#160;DR</a><br>7,600 <small>(6,000 humans, 880 dwarves)</small><sup id=\"cite_ref-DD-p61_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DD-p61-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-tBL-p26_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-tBL-p26-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1359_DR\" title=\"1359 DR\">1359&#160;DR</a><br>1,000&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1357_DR\" title=\"1357 DR\">1357&#160;DR</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Bloodstone_Village\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Bloodstone Village\">Inhabitants of  Bloodstone Village</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Bloodstone_Village\" title=\"Category:Locations in Bloodstone Village\">Locations in  Bloodstone Village</a></nav>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Bloodstone Village</b>, later called <b>Bloodstone City</b><sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and sometimes called <b>Bloodstone Gate</b>,<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p107_2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p107-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> was a settlement in <a href=\"/wiki/Bloodstone_Pass\" title=\"Bloodstone Pass\">Bloodstone Pass</a>, the only real accessible link between the lands of <a href=\"/wiki/Vaasa\" title=\"Vaasa\">Vaasa</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Damara\" title=\"Damara\">Damara</a>. It was within the <a href=\"/wiki/Barony_of_Bloodstone\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Barony of Bloodstone\">Barony of Bloodstone</a><sup id=\"cite_ref-.0_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-.0-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and later became the capital of the <a href=\"/wiki/Kingdom_of_Bloodstone\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Kingdom of Bloodstone\">Kingdom of Bloodstone</a> encompassing Damara and Vaasa. The city was razed in <a href=\"/wiki/1469_DR\" title=\"1469 DR\">1469 DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notes\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notes</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Bloodstone_Village?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The village of Bloodstone lay on the shores of <a href=\"/wiki/Lake_Midai\" title=\"Lake Midai\">Lake Midai</a>, where it joined with the <a href=\"/wiki/Beaumaris_River\" title=\"Beaumaris River\">Beaumaris River</a>, which ran into the <a href=\"/wiki/Galena_Mountains\" title=\"Galena Mountains\">Galena Mountains</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-.0_5-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-.0-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Bloodstone_Village?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n\n<p>Before <a href=\"/wiki/1347_DR\" title=\"1347 DR\">1347 DR</a>,<sup id=\"cite_ref-GHotR-p142_6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GHotR-p142-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Bloodstone Pass was an important trade route, which brought prosperity to Bloodstone Village as the second largest settlement in the Pass. However, when a <a href=\"/wiki/Dragon_turtle\" title=\"Dragon turtle\">dragon turtle</a> was slain in the <a href=\"/wiki/Moonsea_(lake)\" title=\"Moonsea (lake)\">Moonsea</a> to the south that had been terrorized shipping routes, trade by sea was opened to the <a href=\"/wiki/Sea_of_Fallen_Stars\" title=\"Sea of Fallen Stars\">Sea of Fallen Stars</a> and the land route through Bloodstone Pass was less frequented.<sup id=\"cite_ref-.0_5-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-.0-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-BL-p3_7-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BL-p3-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/1347_DR\" title=\"1347 DR\">1347 DR</a>, Bloodstone Village was ravaged by the harsh <a href=\"/wiki/Wolf_Winter\" title=\"Wolf Winter\">Wolf Winter</a>, during which their crops died and starving <a href=\"/wiki/Dire_wolves\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dire wolves\">dire wolves</a> killed 70 of the village's inhabitants.<sup id=\"cite_ref-BL-p4_8-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BL-p4-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-H2-p5_9-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-H2-p5-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Beginning the next year, the Bloodstone Pass became cut off from the rest of the Kingdom of Damara due to the <a href=\"/wiki/Vaasan_War\" title=\"Vaasan War\">war with Vaasa</a> to the north, and the baron of the time, Baron <a href=\"/wiki/Tranth\" title=\"Tranth\">Tranth</a>, had little power over the dominion.<sup id=\"cite_ref-.0_5-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-.0-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Many settlements within the area were reduced to anarachy. In this anarchy came the <a href=\"/wiki/Citadel_of_Assassins\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Citadel of Assassins\">Citadel of Assassins</a> and their hold on the village. Bloodstone Village was forced to pay an annual tribute (two tendays after the annual harvest) in food, money, and slaves.<sup id=\"cite_ref-.0_5-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-.0-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/1359_DR\" title=\"1359 DR\">1359 DR</a>, it became the home of the King of Damara, <a href=\"/wiki/Gareth_Dragonsbane\" title=\"Gareth Dragonsbane\">Gareth Dragonsbane</a>,<sup id=\"cite_ref-.0_5-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-.0-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and the site of the <a href=\"/wiki/Tree-Gem_of_Bloodstone\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tree-Gem of Bloodstone\">Tree-Gem</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-GHotR-p144_10-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GHotR-p144-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Beginning at this time, Baron Tranth began encouraging the King to annex Vaasa to create a unified kingdom of Damara and Vaasa called <i>Bloodstone</i>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-BL-p6_11-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BL-p6-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Before the end of his reign, Gareth Dragonsbane followed through on this idea.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p188_12-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p188-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The capital of this kingdom was later moved from <a href=\"/wiki/Heliogabalus\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Heliogabalus\">Heliogabalus</a> to Bloodstone Village, which by this time had grown to be a large city known as Bloodstone Gate<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p107_2-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p107-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and later Bloodstone City.<sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/1460_DR\" title=\"1460 DR\">1460 DR</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/Warlock_Knights\" title=\"Warlock Knights\">Warlock Knights</a> of Vaasa rebelled against the Kingdom of Bloodstone,<sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.78_13-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.78-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and in <a href=\"/wiki/1469_DR\" title=\"1469 DR\">1469 DR</a>, they burned Bloodstone City to the ground.<sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.78_13-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.78-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-14\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>note 1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> As of <a href=\"/wiki/1480_DR\" title=\"1480 DR\">1480 DR</a>, the site was garrisoned by the Warlock Knights,<sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.80-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and the settlement remained in ruins through the turn of the 16<sup>th</sup> century DR.<sup id=\"cite_ref-HoF-p61_15-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HoF-p61-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Bloodstone_Village?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Abbey_of_St._Sollars\" title=\"Abbey of St. Sollars\">Abbey of St. Sollars</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Lake_Midai\" title=\"Lake Midai\">Lake Midai</a></li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/White_Tree\" title=\"White Tree\">White Tree</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Inn_of_the_Clowns\" title=\"Inn of the Clowns\">Inn of the Clowns</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Bloodstone_Village?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notes\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Bloodstone_Village?veaction=edit&section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notes\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<small><div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-14\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-14\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Canon\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Canon\">Canon</a> material does not provide a precise date for the razing of <a href=\"/wiki/Bloodstone_City\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Bloodstone City\">Bloodstone City</a> in the 15<sup>th</sup> century <a href=\"/wiki/DR\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>. The article \"Realmslore: Vaasa\" in <a href=\"/wiki/Dungeon_magazine_177\" title=\"Dungeon magazine 177\"><i>Dungeon</i> #177</a> states that the event occurred \"a decade past\" (p. 80) as of <a href=\"/wiki/1480_DR\" title=\"1480 DR\">1480&#160;DR</a> (p. 78). This is generally assumed to be <a href=\"/wiki/1469_DR\" title=\"1469 DR\">Year of Splendors Burning, 1469 DR</a>, given its name.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></small>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Bloodstone_Village?veaction=edit&section=6\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-DunMag.177-p.80-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-2\">1.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-3\">1.3</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-4\">1.4</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-5\">1.5</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.80_1-6\">1.6</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Brian_R._James\" title=\"Brian R. James\">Brian R. James</a>&#160;(April 2010). “Realmslore: Vaasa”. In <a href=\"/wiki/C